            is always continuous and bounded on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{G}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution"} convolution
            of two functions is the product of the transforms of each of the functions separately.
          %h2#over_the_circle_and_the_integers Over the circle and the integers
          %p
            In the classical case of
