                    \\underset{y \in \mathbb{R}^n}{\int}
                    f(y) \delta(y-x)  \, d^n y
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{y \in \mathbb{R}^n}{\int}
                    \\underset{k \in \mathbb{R}^n}{\int}
                    f(y) e^{i k \cdot (y-x)}
                    \\, \frac{d^n k}{(2\pi)^n} \, d^n y
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{k \in \mathbb{R}^n}{\int}
                    e^{- i k \cdot x}
                    \\underset{= \widehat{f}(-k) }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\underset{y \in \mathbb{R}^n}{\int}
                    f(y) e^{i k \cdot y}
