                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              which is the statement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+inversion+theorem"} Fourier inversion theorem
              for smooth functions (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierInversion"}
            %p
              (Here in the last step we used
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+integration+variables"} change of integration variables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \mapsto -k
              which introduces one sign
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{n}
              for the new volume form, but another sign
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
