              from the re-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
              of the integration domain. )
            %p
              Equivalently, the above computation shows that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product+of+distributions"} convolution product of distributions
          #PaleyWienerSchwartzTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paley-Wiener-Schwartz+theorem"}> Paley-Wiener-Schwartz theorem
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in \mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R}^n) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+supported+distribution"} compactly supported distribution
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tempered+distribution"} tempered distribution
              by example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactlySupportedDistibutionsAreTemperedDistributions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierTransformOnTemperedDistributions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distribution"} non-singular distribution
              induced from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              that grows at most exponentially.
          #FourierInversionTheoremForDistributions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+inversion+theorem"} Fourier inversion theorem
                for
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
            %p
              The operation of forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{u}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierTransformOnTemperedDistributions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tempered+distributions"} tempered distributions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TemperedDistribution"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo ˇ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi u
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo ˇ
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widecheck{ u } \;\colon\; g \mapsto u\left( \widecheck{g}\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo ˇ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widecheck{g}
              is the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+Fourier+transform"} inverse Fourier transform
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              according to prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierInversion"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierTransformOnTemperedDistributions"}
              this follows immediately from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+inversion+theorem"} Fourier inversion theorem
              for smooth functions (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierInversion"}
          %p
            We have the following distributional generalization of the basic property
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FourierTransformInterchangesPointwiseProductWithConvolution"} (3)
            from prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicPropertiesOfFourierTransformOverCartesianSpaces"}
          #FourierTransformOfDistributionsInterchangesConvolutionOfDistributionsWithPointwiseProduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
                interchanges
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+of+distributions"} convolution of distributions
                with pointwise product)
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u_1 \in \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tempered+distribution"} tempered distribution
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TemperedDistribution"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u_2 \in \mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R}^n) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+supported+distribution"} compactly supported distribution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tempered+distribution"} tempered distribution
              via example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactlySupportedDistibutionsAreTemperedDistributions"}
            %p
              Observe here that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paley-Wiener-Schwartz+theorem"} Paley-Wiener-Schwartz theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PaleyWienerSchwartzTheorem"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distribution"} non-singular distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{u_1} \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              so that the product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{u_1} \cdot \widehat{u_2}
              is always defined.
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product+of+distributions"} convolution product of distributions
              is the product of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⋆
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{u_1 \star u_2}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\widehat{u_1} \cdot \widehat{u_2}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"} Hörmander 90, theorem 7.1.15
          #ProductOfDistributionsViaFourierTransformOfConvolution.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
                via
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierTransformOfDistributionsInterchangesConvolutionOfDistributionsWithPointwiseProduct"}
              together with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+inversion+theorem"} Fourier inversion theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierInversionTheoremForDistributions"}
              %em define
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1 \cdot u_2
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+supported+distributions"} compactly supported distributions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1, u_2 \in \mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R}^n) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
              by the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{ u_1 \cdot u_2 }
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    (2\pi)^n \widehat{u_1} \star \widehat{u_2}
            %p
              which would complete the generalization of of property
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FourierTransformInterchangesPointwiseProductWithConvolution"} (3)
              from prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicPropertiesOfFourierTransformOverCartesianSpaces"}
            %p
              For this to make sense, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product"} convolution product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              on the right needs to exist, which is not guaranteed (prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConvolutionProductOnSchwartzSpace"}
              does not apply here!). The condition that this exists is the
              = succeed "-condition" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+H%C3%B6rmander"} Hörmander
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_2
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
              for more.
